"to redden","H8476":"leather","H4605":"above","H7175":"board","H6086":"wood","H7848":"acacia","H5975":"stand","H2677":"half","H8147":"two","H3027":"hand","H7947":"to fit","H6285":"side","H5045":"Negeb","H8486":"south","H705":"forty","H134":"socket","H3701":"money","H8478":"under","H6763":"side","H6828":"north","H3411":"flank","H3220":"sea","H4742":"corner","H8382":"be double","H4295":"beneath","H3162":"unitedness","H7218":"head","H2885":"ring","H4740":"Angle","H1280":"bar","H8484":"middle","H1272":"to flee","H8432":"midst","H4480":"from","H6823":"to overlay","H1004":"place","H6532":"curtain","H5982":"pillar","H2053":"hook","H3332":"pour","H4539":"covering","H6607":"entrance","H7551":"to weave","H2838":"ring"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Vows, or voluntary oblations to Moses, according to the Hebrew. (Calmet) — These donations are called first-fruits, because they were the best of all things, and the first offerings that were made by the people, in the desert. (Tirinus) — They shew great alacrity in performing this action, as it was to make some atonement for their liberality in honour of the golden calf. (Haydock) — But as matter alone will not suffice, unless it be properly managed, so neither will the letter of the Scripture instruct us, unless God teach us, by his pastors, Ephesians iv. 11. (Worthington) — From this place to the end, the Roman edition of the Septuagint is very confused. That of Alcala agrees better with the Vulgate than the Alexandrian or Aldine. See Grabe. Almost all the three following chapters might be comprised in these words. The workmen did all according to God’s prescription. Moses perhaps gave them plans of what each was to execute; and hence Calmet accounts for these repetitions. (Haydock)"],["haydock",33,null,"haydock","Bar, not mentioned, (chap. xxvi. 28,) but specified by Josephus ([Antiquities?] iii. 5,) at the west end of the tabernacle, going across the breadth of the planks. (Tostat)"],["haydock",38,null,"haydock","Which heads, according to the Hebrew and Septuagint. On some parts of the pillars the wood appeared."]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}